      "id": "SEL-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Why a unit determinant pays for q to the complex rank",
      "anchor": "inputs-selmer-kernel",
      "statement": "Let C be the ideal class group modulo δ=(γ⁻¹−a) and E the integral unit group modulo the image of δ and all roots of unity. |EqHom|≤|C|ℓ, |W|=|E||C| and |E|(a−1)=(a^n−1)^r₂. Consequently |EqHom| q^r₂ ≤ |W|ℓ ℓ^(c+f), with f=vℓ(e).",
      "hypotheses": "Totally complex fixed base field L′; γ generates Gal(F/L′) and acts on a primitive ℓ^ν-th root by 1+ℓ^c; n=ord γ=ℓ^(ν−c), 1≤c≤ν, c≥2 when ℓ=2, a=(1+ℓ^c)^e with e≥1, q=ℓ^ν, r₂ the number of complex places of L′. All divisor and class groups here belong to the upper field F.",
