      "correspondence": "A character's extension to the divisor group kills principal divisors and δ of any divisor. Evaluate on singleton primes to recover the original function. For finite class group the kernel and cokernel of δ have equal orders. The modulus-free determinant calculation adjoins a trivial ℤ-line to log units, giving r₂ full cycles of length n and an auxiliary (a−1) factor on the constant line. Applying LTE gives vℓ(|E|)+c+f=(ν+f)r₂, and weakening (ν+f)r₂≥νr₂ accounts for the factor in the stated inequality.",
      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "review": "Checked the gamma inverse on divisors and units, finite character bound, both valuations and the determinant factor from the extra line. Small example at ℓ=3,c=2,e=3,ν=3 has v₃(1000−1)=3 and v₃(1000³−1)=4."
