      "correspondence": "The two orders a^n−1 and q have valuation difference f independent of ν. The telescoping relation yields an annihilator ℓ^b(a^n−1)/q for ker f_norm and hence exponent ≤ℓ^(b+f) on its ℓ-part. Bound |W[ℓ^s]| inductively by |W[ℓ]|^s. An invariant class determines a root-of-unity exponent mod ℓ and an ℓth root of a fixed norm in L′; together these allow at most ℓ² choices. Hilbert 90 and unramified valuations away from ℓ show each fiber is covered by the base-field Selmer classes. At the base, units, ℓ-killed ideal classes and the valuations at primes dividing ℓ give bounds ℓ^D, ℓ^⌊log₂ h⌋ and ℓ^D. The two ℓ-adic costs and the image size now combine exactly as sCount.",
      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "review": "The comparison concerns the ℓ-primary portion of the kernel. The full annihilator may contain a prime-to-ℓ factor. The norm used for the pair (t,Norm(v)) is the ordinary field norm, distinct from the powered twisted norm used by Few."
